    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "The guiding principle: act with urgency and go after the opponent's single most vulnerable piece — his knight — before he ever completes development. If you let those pieces out, the initiative simply evaporates.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "When your edge is time, attack the opponent's weakest piece immediately; don't finish your own development first.",
